{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And now, behold I…</b> Meaning, he is ready to fulfill the decree of the King to go at that time. And he used singular language corresponding to what he alluded to him in the word ״לְךָ״ as I explained, and he said <b>to my people</b> corresponding to what he said to him, ״to your place״; but concerning the detail of fleeing, he did not concede to him, for he was not afraid of him since he was a great sorcerer — and go out and learn (Midrash HaGadol on Numbers 31:8) how mighty the children of Israel had to be together with him in order to kill him, and all the more so others who could not do him any harm." "<b>that this people shall do… in the end…</b> Meaning, since he wished to reveal to him that Israel would destroy and uproot the seed of Moav, and Balak as well perhaps saw this matter in the bird, for the children of Israel would crush the borders of Moav, therefore he said to him that what this people shall do to your people will be in the end of days. And the reason it was necessary to inform him of this matter is because he came to counsel him the counsel of sending out their daughters, as they said, of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 106a), in explanation of his saying ״לְכָה אִיעָצְךָ״ — therefore he was concerned that he would say: how is it possible that their women would go out to the children of Israel who are coming to destroy them? Would not anyone who goes out be stabbed? Therefore he informed him that this people would not do harm or destruction to your people until the end of days, and their women could go out to the camp of Israel according to his counsel. And he was precise in saying <b>to your people</b>, to say specifically to your people, who are Moav, over whom he was king — that they would do nothing to them except in the end of days, but excluding Balak, for he would be suddenly broken, as indeed was the case, as it is written (Numbers 31:8) ״וְאֶת מַלְכֵי מִדְיָן״ etc., and he was one of them, as they said, of blessed memory (Bemidbar Rabbah 22:20)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:13:57.974889517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}